<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khoy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khoy is a city in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a> and near the Turkish border. It lay on the trade route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaldiran">Battle of Chaldiran</a> was fought north-west of it in 1514. From the Safavid period the Kurdish Donboli family held hereditary authority there, ruling it as a khanate after 1747 until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a> absorbed it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khoy.jpg" alt="Khoy" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sina-agheshlouei · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arg_hokumati_xoy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
